      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7463011935245217793?commentUrn=urn%3Ali%3Acomment%3A(activity%3A7463011935245217793%2C7463380851616075777)",
      "text": "This is becoming the real distortion. Hiring managers increasingly expect candidates to arrive already able to use GenAI properly, research faster, prepare better, automate parts of their own work, and operate above the level they are being paid for. So the market wants a strange bargain. Someone who can carry a role two levels higher, accept a smaller title, and treat the salary bump as a gift. The company sees efficiency. The candidate sees opp",
